                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُتْعَةٌ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>Enjoyment;</i> a subst. in the sense of
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَتُّعٌ</span>; (S, Msb, K;) syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَعْمَةٌ</span>. (Jel, xlvi. 26.)
See an ex., in a verse of Lebeed, voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَرْطٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُتْعَةٌ</span>
                        <i>A gift to a divorced wife.</i> (Msb, K.) See
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَتَاعٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">متعة الضُّحَى</span> [i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُتْعَة</span>?] <i>i. q.</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَوَّلُهَا</span>.
(TA voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِيقَة</span>, in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فوق</span>.)

